Mesa Custom Build Guide (Haswell + Niri/Wayland)
1. Preparation & Dependencies

Ensure the necessary build tools and Python modules are installed:
Bash

# Core Build Tools
sudo pacman -S meson ninja gcc cmake pkgconf

# Mesa Dependencies (Arch specific)
sudo pacman -S wayland-protocols libglvnd libdrm libudev-static libclc spirv-llvm-translator expat

# Python Modules for Code Generation
sudo pacman -S python-mako python-yaml python-ply

2. Environment Variables

Set these to target the Haswell architecture specifically.
Bash

export CFLAGS="-O2 -march=haswell -pipe -ftree-vectorize"
export CXXFLAGS="-O2 -march=haswell -pipe -ftree-vectorize"

3. The Build Configuration (The "Golden" Flags)

This configuration targets Haswell hardware, enables Wayland, and ensures XWayland compatibility.
Bash

# Clean previous attempts
rm -rf build/

# Configure the build
meson setup build/ \
  --prefix=/usr \
  --libdir=lib \
  --buildtype=release \
  -Doptimization=2 \
  -Db_lto=false \
  -Dplatforms=wayland,x11 \
  -Dglx=dri \
  -Dgallium-drivers=crocus,zink,llvmpipe \
  -Dvulkan-drivers=intel_hasvk \
  -Dopengl=true \
  -Dgles1=disabled \
  -Dgles2=enabled \
  -Degl=enabled \
  -Dgbm=enabled \
  -Dllvm=enabled \
  -Dshared-llvm=enabled \
  -Dvideo-codecs=all

4. Build and Install
Bash

# Compile (using all CPU threads)
ninja -C build

# Install and Strip (removes debug symbols for a lean binary)
sudo meson install -C build --strip

# Refresh dynamic linker cache
sudo ldconfig

5. Maintenance (Post-Install)

To prevent Arch Linux from overwriting your custom build during a system update:

    Open /etc/pacman.conf

    Add the following to the IgnorePkg line: IgnorePkg = mesa lib32-mesa vulkan-intel

6. Verification

Run these commands to confirm your custom build is active:

    OpenGL: glxinfo | grep "Mesa 26.1.0-devel"

    Vulkan: vulkaninfo --summary | grep hasvk




RUSTFLAGS="-C target-cpu=haswell -C opt-level=z -C linker=clang -C link-arg=-fuse-ld=lld" \
                                  CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_LTO=fat \
                                  CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_CODEGEN_UNITS=1 \
                                  CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_PANIC=abort \
                                  cargo build --release






RUSTFLAGS="-C target-cpu=haswell -C lto=thin -C codegen-units=1" cargo build --release

export KCFLAGS="-march=haswell"

RUSTFLAGS="-C target-cpu=haswell -C lto=thin -C codegen-units=1" cargo build --release --features systemd


sudo setcap 'cap_sys_nice=eip' $(which niri)

sudo nice -n -5 niri --session

sudo renice -n -5 -p $(pidof niri)
